# Once DolphinFile pool exhaustion became a recoverable nlOpen failure, audio
# streams could retain a null file while claiming to be initialized. A queued
# track would later finish fading out its predecessor, call Warm, and pass that
# null file to nlSeek. The crash wrote through address 0xC.
#
# Report Open failure in the stream state, discard a failed queued track before
# it can replace the active one, and let random crowd streams retry on a later
# update. This also handles genuinely missing stream files without crashing.
